## 2. Mandatory Page Creation Workflow (`nextjs-page-dev`)

Whenever you are asked to create, scaffold, build, or implement **any new Next.js App Router page or route (`page.tsx`)**:

1. **Always Activate & Read First**: You **MUST** read and follow [`.agents/skills/nextjs-page-dev/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/nextjs-page-dev/SKILL.md) before writing any route or page files.
2. **Non-Negotiable Standards from `nextjs-page-dev`**:
   - **Planning & Route Registry**: Resolve `supported_languages`, `dictionaries_dir`, and `new_component_dir` from `docs/project.json` and use `ROUTES` from `@/lib/routes`.
   - **Zero Hardcoded Copy**: Populate page titles, meta descriptions, and copy in `messages/[locale].json` across all supported locales before writing JSX.
   - **Companion Route Files**: Create `loading.tsx` skeleton and `error.tsx` boundary where applicable.
   - **Page Implementation (`page.tsx`)**: Use async `params` (`Promise<{ locale: string, ... }>`), export `generateMetadata()` with canonical alternates, export `generateStaticParams()` for localized/dynamic routes, inject typed `<JsonLd>` (`schema-dts`) with `<` escaped as `\u003c`, and wrap dynamic streaming subtrees in granular `<Suspense>` boundaries.
   - **Delegate New Page Components to `nextjs-component-dev`**: Whenever a new page requires new section or child components, you **MUST** use [`.agents/skills/nextjs-component-dev/SKILL.md`](./.agents/skills/nextjs-component-dev/SKILL.md) to build each component.
   - **Verification Gate**: Run `pwsh .agents/skills/nextjs-page-dev/scripts/verify-page.ps1 -RoutePath <route_dir>`.
   - **Plan Checklist Sync**: Check off completed page infrastructure items (`page.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `generateMetadata`, `JSON-LD Schema`, `generateStaticParams()`) in `docs/plan/05-pages-and-components.md`, and check off the parent page item when all its sub-items are complete.

